  "description": "Flat at 300, sea 250. GetWaterType at a vertex whose depth is NaN gives 2 (TR6). AltitudeAtWhichFloodingWillOccur(5, 5): the vertex dry, W wet at level 260 (alt 250, depth 10) and E wet at 255 -> 260; all neighbours dry -> 250 (the sea level); a wet vertex below the sea level does not raise it; its own level counts when wet and above (alt 200, depth 70 -> 270); the corner vertex's mask keeps its neighbours inside (TR3). GetLerpedWaterLevel (5.1): 250 over dry flat ground (level = alt + depth); NaN in a cell with the NaN corner (2, 2); at (72, 80), halfway between (4, 5) at 260 and (5, 5) at 250 -> 255; x < 0 -> 0. GetWaterVelocity: no flow, a zero vector; GetSedimentValue(x, z): 0 in bounds, 0 out of bounds (TR12).",
